@startwbs
!include style-plantuml.puml
title Docker file hierarchy

<style>
wbsDiagram {
  .repo {
    BackgroundColor #fff/lawngreen
  }
  .in-scope-dir {
    BackgroundColor #fff/blue
  }
  .in-scope-file {
    BackgroundColor #fff/blue
  }
  .oos-dir {
    BackgroundColor #fff/aaf
  }
  .oos-file {
    BackgroundColor #fff/aaf
  }
}
</style>

+ Repository <<repo>>
++ docker/ <<in-scope-dir>>
+++ README.adoc <<in-scope-file>>
+++ docker-xxx/ <<in-scope-dir>>
++++ README.adoc <<in-scope-file>>
++++ Dockerfile <<in-scope-file>>
++++ docker/ <<in-scope-dir>>
+++++ file xxx <<in-scope-file>>
+++++ file yyy <<in-scope-file>>
++ documentation/ <<oos-dir>>
+++ ADR/ <<oos-dir>>
++++ ADR-029-container-security.adoc <<oos-file>>
++ scripts/ <<oos-dir>>

legend
    Each Docker image definition:
    * has a readme
    ** is included in a higher level readme
    * separates the Dockerfile from the files that are copied to the image
end legend

@endwbs
